  "Founded in 1995 by Wang Chuanfu as a rechargeable battery manufacturer in Shenzhen; it entered car making in 2003 by buying a struggling state automaker. Wang is still chairman and CEO. BYD is now the largest producer of electric and plug-in hybrid vehicles in the world, and it is vertically integrated to an extreme degree — it makes its own Blade batteries, semiconductors, motors and electronics. That integration is why it can undercut competitors on price. It also builds electric buses, and Warren Buffett's Berkshire Hathaway was an early shareholder.",
